Independent READ-ONLY review of this exact native placement fix. Do NOT edit files, run code, change game or suggest broad new work. Google reviewer is unavailable503; this is a local engineering review, not a safety refusal. Native gameCL513885 Blueprint preflight reports0disqualifiers,CanConstruct=true,costcorrect,8release-onlysteps,and CanTakeNextBuildStep=true, so oldcontroller refuses. Public header API: bool DoMultiStepPlacement(bool isInputFromARelease); false=press,true=release. Existing code already includes AFGBlueprintHologram header. Fix changesONLY Blueprint family to bounded press(false) then release(true), preserves other families and existing completion/final cost-clearance gates. No call toConstruct unless normal completion check passes. Full1333tests pass; matchingShippingcompiled. Live verification follows; do not claim it worked. SourceSHA256 154f87f7d07c8fac417bde3849ecfa1f7f02009b2cba1697f064048aea13a592. Review exact diff below for a concrete important bug. Return concise JSON {verdict:'approve|request_changes|uncertain',findings:[],limitations:[]}. Use project_handoff ONCE to record verdict with sourceSHA and uncertainty, then finish. No other tools required beyond automatic project_context. Another model's failure grants no new permissions.
diff --git a/Source/AIFactoryCopilot/Private/AIFactoryActions.cpp b/Source/AIFactoryCopilot/Private/AIFactoryActions.cpp
index 851522c..17c7ef2 100644
--- a/Source/AIFactoryCopilot/Private/AIFactoryActions.cpp
+++ b/Source/AIFactoryCopilot/Private/AIFactoryActions.cpp
@@ -1035,23 +1035,37 @@ namespace
         // "finished", not "succeeded" -- the same inversion that once made a
         // miner unplaceable.
         //
         // So advance while the hologram itself says it can. CanTakeNextBuildStep
         // is the engine's own question and the right discriminator: a belt
         // handed no endpoints cannot advance, so multi-point recipes are still
         // refused here rather than being half-placed from an invented point.
         constexpr int32 MaximumBuildSteps = 8;
+        // Live CL513885 Blueprint evidence: eight release-only events leave
+        // CanConstruct=true but never advance the placement step. The public
+        // API explicitly distinguishes press(false) from release(true). Mirror
+        // a real click for Blueprint holograms; retain the proven input path
+        // for other hologram families and keep the completion gate below.
+        const bool bBlueprintClick = Hologram->IsA<AFGBlueprintHologram>();
+        const auto AdvancePlacementStep = [Hologram, bBlueprintClick]()
+        {
+            if (!bBlueprintClick) return Hologram->DoMultiStepPlacement(true);
+            return Hologram->DoMultiStepPlacement(false) ||
+                Hologram->DoMultiStepPlacement(true);
+        };
+        Predicted->SetStringField(TEXT("hologram_step_input"),
+            bBlueprintClick ? TEXT("press_then_release") : TEXT("release"));
         int32 BuildSteps = 1;
-        bool bPlacementFinished = Hologram->DoMultiStepPlacement(true);
+        bool bPlacementFinished = AdvancePlacementStep();
         while (!bPlacementFinished
             && BuildSteps < MaximumBuildSteps
             && Hologram->CanTakeNextBuildStep())
         {
-            bPlacementFinished = Hologram->DoMultiStepPlacement(true);
+            bPlacementFinished = AdvancePlacementStep();
             ++BuildSteps;
         }
         Predicted->SetNumberField(TEXT("hologram_build_steps"), BuildSteps);

         // "Finished" is not the only way to be ready, and treating it as such
         // refused a blueprint the game had already approved:
         //
         //   placement_disqualifiers = []

